# Copy to .test.env (gitignored) to run `make regression-live CONFIRM=1` against a real switch.
# The only value accepted for a real switch is sw03 (the label of the target the suite may write to);
# the label sw01 is refused by name, and so is any host listed in TPLINK_REGRESSION_READONLY_HOSTS.
TPLINK_REGRESSION_TARGET=sw03
TPLINK_REGRESSION_HOST=192.0.2.13
TPLINK_REGRESSION_USERNAME=admin
TPLINK_REGRESSION_PASSWORD=
# Ports a scenario may change: free, link-down, in no LAG. The scenarios need four; LAG scenarios put the
# second and the third (and, in one refusal case, the first, with the first protected port) in LAG
# group 1, which takes ports 1 to 4 only, so those ports must lie in that range.
TPLINK_REGRESSION_TEST_PORTS=2,3,4,5
# The port that carries management traffic (listed first) and the ports that carry a device: named
# only by guard-refusal scenarios. The guard scenarios need the first and three more.
TPLINK_REGRESSION_PROTECTED_PORTS=1,6,7,8
# Addresses of switches that must never be a target, comma separated.
TPLINK_REGRESSION_READONLY_HOSTS=192.0.2.11
# Optional: also move the switch to a spare address and back (the management-move scenario).
# The address must be free (outside the DHCP pool, nothing bound to it); it is never probed before the move.
# TPLINK_REGRESSION_ALLOW_MANAGEMENT_MOVE=1
# TPLINK_REGRESSION_MOVE_IP=192.0.2.14
# Optional: also turn DHCP on and back off through the provider, with the switch named by its MAC address
# only (the DHCP scenario). The router must have a DHCP server up: the switch takes the address it gives.
# TPLINK_REGRESSION_ALLOW_DHCP=1
# Optional: let the allow_disruptive scenario write to a port that carries a device (a brief link drop).
# TPLINK_REGRESSION_DISRUPT_DEVICE_PORT=8
# Optional: the device ports the disruptive scenarios may change for real (a speed change, a port taken
# down, a LAG, a mirror destination, a VLAN group with a device port). Never the management port (the
# first protected port). Expect the devices behind these ports to lose the network for a while.
# TPLINK_REGRESSION_DISRUPTIVE_PORTS=7,8
